From f133056b6d84defc9c5a7a739eccc01adc0d42d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:44:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): resume re-checks inside unblock's write txn;
 recovery card must postdate the park; imperative-only authority regex
 [daveey]

Review of d104444: preflight ran outside the unblock transaction, so a
needs_input ask landing mid-drain was released and its human_request erased
(reproduced). unblock_task gains precondition=, evaluated first under BEGIN
IMMEDIATE; resume passes its full refusal check there.

Also: an ancestor may only be resumed by a card created after its current
continuation_exhausted park; the authority regex matches imperative asks only
(kanban_unblock, un-block, move .. to ready, release/reopen, raise the
continuation limit) and no longer refuses history like 'was unblocked by t_x';
a legacy authority repair's refusal names the archive escape; readback faults
after a committed apply are reported, not swallowed.
---
